From d3ccf690c19e5ed8943abca11f99f47b907b5f2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juup <pikkemaatjuup@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:10:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mx: native OCP-MX (mxfp4a8/mxfp8a8/mxfp6a8), int5, ParoQuant
 Path A

Squashed feature branch rebased onto radiance 1.2.3. Contents:

- Native OCP-MX weight family on qwen35: mxfp4a8 / mxfp8a8 / mxfp6a8 GEMMs
  (skinny decode + tiled prefill), MX layout/relayout/unrelayout hooks, E4M3
  activation with a per-row f32 scale, no b_ref for the self-scaling fp8/fp6
  codebooks, and the ArchQuant plumbing that selects them.
- Dense signed-5-bit (int5 / w5a8) weight family on the same activation grid.
- ParoQuant Path A: givens-rotated fp6 weights served in place, the host
  encoding oracle (enc_givens_forward) with tests, the standalone and fused
  per-partition producers (paroquant_quant_fp8_row, ..._rmsnorm_quant_fp8_row2/3,
  ..._gated_quant_fp8_row1), the partition-select gemm_nt_q_paro op
  (gemm_mxfp6a8_paro_nt_m64 / _tiled) that runs a merged weight as a single GEMM
  launch whose output-column partitions take different activations, the
  paroquant-aware encoding/layout acceptance gated on the quant id, the
  rad-convert container writer that preserves the rotation tables, and the
  qwen35_paroquant architecture.
- Serving/runtime ports: E4M3 embedding, int5 and drafter options, M-banded
  decode hybrid, adaptive per-sequence verify length for the block drafter,
  opt-in f16 GDN state, tape/dispatch-trace diagnostics, server stop-string
  scoping, and the MX AR-fold runtime switch (default off).
- Device selftests for every new kernel family.

Path A currently wins on quality (mean KLD 0.0053 vs Path B 0.0091); closing
the decode-throughput gap is a follow-up.
